      "content": "Originalism is a legal philosophy that interprets the Constitution based on the original intent or meaning of the Founding Fathers. Proponents argue that this approach preserves the Constitution's integrity and prevents judges from imposing their personal views. Living constitutionalism, on the other hand, views the Constitution as a dynamic document that should evolve with societal changes. Advocates believe this approach allows for a more relevant and just application of the law. In the case of the Second Amendment, originalists argue that it was intended to protect the right to bear arms for a well-regulated militia, while living constitutionalists contend that it should be interpreted in the context of modern society, potentially allowing for more regulation of firearms.",
