      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for that, but it feels like the explanation for Living Constitutionalism is still a bit circular—it keeps saying it \"adapts to societal changes\" without explaining the actual judicial mechanism used to do so. \n\nOn the other hand, the Originalist explanation is much more structurally grounded in textualism and intent. If I were writing a paper on the most logically robust method for judicial restraint, which of these frameworks provides a more consistent, predictable application of the law that prevents subjective policymaking by judges?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
